# Variables
# Demonstrates file variables, environment variables, and variable substitution

### File variables (local to this file)
@baseUrl = https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com
@postId = 1
@timeout = 30s

###

### Using file variables
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}

###

### Multiple file variables
@userId = 5
@limit = 10

GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?userId={{userId}}&_limit={{limit}}

###

### System/environment variables
# These can be set in your OS environment or in a .env file
# Use {{VAR}} or {{$env VAR}} syntax — both work the same

GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{$env USERNAME}}

###

### Mixed variables: file + environment + expression
@version = v1

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{version}}/posts/{{postId}}

###

### Note about variable precedence (highest to lowest):
# 1. System environment variables
# 2. .env file (if present)
# 3. File variables (@var = value)

# Example with .env file:
# If your workspace has a .env file with:
#   API_KEY=secret123
#   API_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# You can use:
# Authorization: Bearer {{API_KEY}}
# GET {{API_URL}}/resource
